(a) No person shall permit or cause a vehicle registered in his/her name to park contrary to any provision of this article. If the identity of the operator of a vehicle used or parked contrary to this article cannot be determined, the name of the person listed as the owner of the vehicle with the state department of motor vehicles shall be prima facie evidence that the registered owner was the operator of the vehicle.
(b) Whenever an officer observes an unattended vehicle that is parked contrary to any provision of this article, he shall attach to the vehicle a notice informing the operator or owner that the vehicle has been parked contrary to the provisions of this article. The notice shall include the following information:
(1) The location where the vehicle is parked;
(2) The state registration or license number of the vehicle;
(3) The date and time that the officer observed the vehicle parked or operated contrary to the provisions of this article;
(4) A statement that if the owner or operator of the vehicle does not submit payment of an improper parking charge within 14 days after the notice is placed on the vehicle, the owner of the vehicle may be served with a summons to appear in municipal court to answer to charges of violating this article;
(5) A statement that if the owner or operator wishes to challenge or contest the charges of violating this article before the municipal court, he may do so; and
(6) Any other facts which the officer may determine necessary for a thorough understanding of the circumstances.
(c) Officers shall have the authority to issue notices to any vehicle parked contrary to the provisions of this article or to issue a citation to any owner or operator of any vehicle parked contrary to the provisions of this article. Officers shall have the authority to issue notices by using either: (1) a pre-printed notice form to be filled in manually by the officer; or (2) an electronic device that produces a single paper copy of the notice to be issued. An electronic record or memory of the notice issued by an officer using an electronic device shall be maintained. Any paper printout of that electronic record or memory of the notice shall be prima facie evidence that it is a valid copy of the original notice issued.
(d) The operator or owner of a vehicle receiving a notice that the vehicle was observed by an officer to be parked contrary to the provisions of this article shall submit full payment of the appropriate improper parking charge within 14 days of the time the notice was attached to the vehicle by placing the required sum of money in the envelope attached to the notice and: (1) delivering the notice envelope and payment to the city police department; or (2) mailing the notice envelope and payment to the City of Waynesboro at 628 Myrick Street, Waynesboro, Georgia 30830. The amount of the improper parking charge shall be as follows:
(1) The improper parking charge shall be $20.00 regularly or $30.00 if issued in an area designated by the city council as an "enhanced penalty" area;
(2) For violation of section 103-59(i) of this article, the improper parking charge shall be $250.00.
(e) The failure, neglect, or refusal of an owner or operator to submit full payment of an improper parking charge within 14 days of the time the notice was attached to the vehicle owned or operated by him shall be unlawful and constitute a violation of this article.
(f) The chief of police shall have the authority, at any time after the expiration of the 14 day period from the attachment of the notice to the vehicle or the issuance of a towing notice, but before a court summons has been issued, to send or cause to be sent notice(s) informing the owner of the vehicle that late penalty fees shall be assessed against him, unless the owner has submitted a written request to the municipal court asking that a hearing be scheduled regarding the violation of this article.
(g) The amount of the initial late penalty fee for each violation shall be equal to the improper parking charge for such violation. The amount of the late penalty fee shall include any towing charge that was initially assessed.
(h) If an owner or operator fails, neglects, or refuses to make full payment of the improper parking charge or towing charge, within 14 days of the time the notice was attached to the vehicle or the date that the towing notice was issued, then the chief of police, or an officer, may issue a summons to the operator or owner of the vehicle used in violation of this article to appear in court to answer to charges of violating this article.
(i) Any person found by a court of law to be guilty of a violation of this article shall be required to pay:
(1) For failure to pay the improper parking charge assessed, the minimum fine shall be $50.00 and the maximum fine shall not be more than $500.00;
(2) For failure to pay the improper parking charge assessed under of section 103-59(i) of this article, the minimum fine shall be $510.00 and the maximum fine shall not be more than $1,000.00;
(3) For failure to pay a towing charge assessed, the minimum fine shall be $110.00 and the maximum fine shall not be more than $500.00.
(Ord. No. 2016-02-02, § 2, 3-21-2016)

673:
(a) In the event that the chief of police or his designee determines that it is necessary to cause the removal, towage and storage of a vehicle parked contrary to the provisions of this article, the owner shall be required to pay a towing charge.
